WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.708
Install the UI extra. Then run kd-ui with a workspace directory.

00:00:07.708 --> 00:00:09.625
Open the full printed URL, including its #token part. Keep the terminal
open.

00:00:09.625 --> 00:00:13.125
The first page has no data selected. Filter the catalog for burgers.

00:00:13.125 --> 00:00:14.167
Click the burgers row to load the bundled one-dimensional field.

00:00:14.167 --> 00:00:16.792
Inspect the default field heatmap and its coordinates.

00:00:16.792 --> 00:00:17.833
Next, click Continue to Prepare at the top right.

00:00:17.833 --> 00:00:21.333
For this clean dataset, keep finite differences and no smoothing.

00:00:21.333 --> 00:00:23.333
Click Continue to Search to choose an algorithm and its parameters.

00:00:23.333 --> 00:00:30.542
Compatible modes are preselected. Keep only sga default for this first run.

00:00:30.542 --> 00:00:33.167
Set generations to 20. This controls how many search generations KD runs.

00:00:33.167 --> 00:00:35.667
Set Seeds to 0 for this example. Leave the other algorithm parameters
unchanged.

00:00:35.667 --> 00:00:40.667
Set a 4 GiB memory cap and a two-minute time budget for this run.

00:00:40.667 --> 00:00:42.167
Click Check settings to validate this configuration.

00:00:42.167 --> 00:00:43.583
Click Queue 1 run to start the search.

00:00:43.583 --> 00:00:45.125
The queued job appears below. Click its job link to open live progress.

00:00:45.125 --> 00:00:54.125
Watch the generation counter, the best equation so far and the score curve.

00:00:54.125 --> 00:00:55.833
The run is complete. Click Open result to inspect the sealed equation.

00:00:55.833 --> 00:00:59.208
Read the fitted equation and coefficients. The scores here describe this
completed run.

00:00:59.208 --> 00:01:02.750
Click Fit to inspect the convergence curve and the generated figures.

00:01:02.750 --> 00:01:06.875
Scroll to Field comparison: observed data, the discovered law integrated,
and their difference.

00:01:06.875 --> 00:01:11.125
Return to Verify and click Compute under Forward simulation for a separate
check.

00:01:11.125 --> 00:01:14.042
The forward error is now available. Read it separately from term ablation
and block dispersion.

00:01:14.042 --> 00:01:18.208
Click Report to read or download the HTML report for this same run.

00:01:18.208 --> 00:01:21.000
Your run is saved. Restart kd-ui with the same workspace to return to it
later.
